{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense alternatives analyst. You weigh options for a team lead without inventing evidence or clearing review flags.\nYour personal goal is: Compare two or three candidate actions on evidence, applicability and severity fit."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Compare 2-3 materially different candidate actions for this topic. If the draft proposes an action, include it as the incumbent candidate (incumbent true) with its action_type, instruction, draft_text and rationale copied exactly; include NO_ACTION when observing is plausible. For each operational candidate state intervention_need (kind, why intervening now is needed, evidence) and rate need_strength, temporal_scope (does every current claim rest on current, in-scope sources?), proportionality (is the step proportionate to the evidence and impact?) and list unresolved_assumptions. A source need not literally prescribe a recommendation; a clarification or referral is not wrong merely because questions remain. Set decision: KEEP_INCUMBENT, REPLACE_INCUMBENT (prefer a different candidate that is clearly better) or CLOSE_CALL (close_call true; no winner). For each, cite only evidence_ids present in the evidence provided, and rate evidence support, applicability (current versus historical-only sources) and fit with the assessed severity. Do not invent evidence, outcomes or causes. Refer to people by role (a tutor, the team lead), never by name. Write instruction (one concrete sentence telling the team lead what to do), draft_text (the copyable draft) and rationale (why it helps) in plain words, with no evidence IDs or field names. Name a preferred candidate only if it is clearly better; otherwise set close_call true. Your selection does not resolve the review triggers listed; a team lead decides.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_abd05f6abf50117f\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_abd05f6abf50117f/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Rubric alignment on significant factual errors\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_953da9c9fb3c542a10ba503d\", \"member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"member_c6c1dd006877c443863522d1\"]}, \"draft\": {\"contract_version\": \"agent3-advisor-draft-v11\", \"summary\": \"Two tutors ask what makes a factual error significant; a QA tutor reports that an example labeled minor changes the final recommendation. Current guidance defines significance by whether the error changes the central conclusion or actionable answer; the reported example still lacks the context requested for assessment.\", \"summary_sentences\": [{\"text\": \"Two tutors ask what makes a factual error significant; a QA tutor reports that an example labeled minor changes the final recommendation.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c1\", \"c2\"], \"depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"Current guidance defines significance by whether the error changes the central conclusion or actionable answer; the reported example still lacks the context requested for assessment.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c7\", \"c8\"], \"depends_on\": []}], \"detail_sentences\": [{\"text\": \"In the first tutor's thread, a tutor reports that a wrong date changes event order and says the original question is needed to judge whether the fact is central.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c3\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"In the later tutor's thread, a tutor reports that a year is off by one without changing the recommendation, and a QA tutor asks whether correcting the error would change the answer a user acts on.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c4\", \"c5\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"In the QA tutor's thread, a QA tutor asks whether the date is essential or background context; the question and incorrect fact requested by the team lead have not been provided in the retrieved messages.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c5\", \"c6\", \"c8\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"Earlier approval and outcome records concern batch-14 tie calibration, with improved agreement limited to its reviewed sample; they do not establish an exception to the factual-error criterion for this batch.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c9\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}], \"reasoning\": \"The repeated significance questions and the QA tutor's reported discrepancy support a focused reminder using the existing criterion, without deciding the incomplete examples. The current instructions and FAQ agree. The follow-up retrieval returned earlier tie-calibration records, not a decision settling these factual-error examples; their limited outcome does not justify predicting a benefit for this batch. The QA-thread request remains thread-scoped, and neither retrieved announcement establishes handling for this topic.\", \"claims\": [{\"claim_id\": \"c1\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"Two tutors ask how large a factual error must be to count as significant.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c2\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that a rubric example calls an error minor even though it changes the final recommendation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c3\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"In the first tutor's thread, a tutor reports that a wrong date changes which event happened first, considers that central, and says the evaluator needs the original question to judge centrality.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c4\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"In the later tutor's thread, a tutor reports that the year is off by one but the recommendation would not change.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U012\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c5\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether the date is essential or background context in the QA tutor's thread, and asks whether correcting the error changes the answer a user acts on in the later tutor's thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c6\", \"kind\": \"THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the QA tutor's thread, the team lead requests the question and incorrect fact to determine whether the fact drives the final answer.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"}], \"quote\": \"Share the question and the incorrect fact. We need to know whether that fact drives the final answer.\", \"quote_kind\": \"VERBATIM\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c7\", \"kind\": \"GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current instructions and the FAQ define a significant or major factual error by its effect on the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on; nonessential background errors without that effect are minor.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\"], \"attributions\": [], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c8\", \"kind\": \"INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The retrieved QA tutor's thread ends with the team lead's request for the question and incorrect fact; those inputs and a final assessment of the reported example are not present.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"THREAD_STARTER\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c9\", \"kind\": \"HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier approval covers a batch-14 tie-calibration exercise, not a new numerical threshold. The earlier outcome records increased agreement from two to seven of eight reviewed pairs, limits that benefit to the sample, and says a new batch needs its own evidence. These records do not establish an exception to the factual-error criterion for batch 15.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:053fe48a\"], \"attributions\": [], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c10\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The batch-15 announcement concerns factuality versus instruction adherence and asks for examples in its thread; the batch-14 announcement concerns tie calibration and asks for both rationales at its eight-pair review. Neither establishes handling for the factual-error significance questions here.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790936513.000019:8237860f\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\"], \"attributions\": [], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}], \"gaps\": [{\"gap_id\": \"g1\", \"need\": \"PRIOR_DECISION_OUTCOME\", \"description\": \"The history search returned batch-14 tie-calibration approval and outcome records, not an earlier decision or outcome settling significant factual errors or the reported minor example. Earlier handling of that example remains unestablished; the proposed reminder does not depend on it.\", \"follow_up\": null}, {\"gap_id\": \"g2\", \"need\": \"OTHER\", \"description\": \"The question and incorrect fact requested in the QA tutor's thread are missing from the retrieved messages, so the reported example cannot yet be assessed against the current criterion.\", \"follow_up\": null}], \"evidence_sufficiency\": \"SUFFICIENT\", \"proposed_action\": {\"action_type\": \"POST_ALIGNMENT\", \"intervention_need\": {\"kind\": \"UNRESOLVED_HANDLING_QUESTION\", \"statement\": \"Two tutors separately ask the same significance question without a settled answer in their threads, while a QA tutor reports a mismatch between an example's grade and its effect on the recommendation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\"]}, \"instruction\": \"Post a reminder explaining the current factual-error criterion, without assigning grades to the incomplete examples discussed in the threads.\", \"rationale\": \"The repeated scoring questions call for a shared answer, and the current instructions and FAQ already provide one. A reminder can explain that criterion without treating the reported example as an established exception.\", \"draft_text\": \"A significant factual error changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on. A nonessential background error without that effect is minor.\\n\\nTwo tutors asked about significance. The examples include a tutor's report that a wrong date changes event order, a tutor's report that a one-year error leaves the recommendation unchanged, and a QA tutor's report that an example labeled minor changes the recommendation. These reports alone do not settle the examples' grades.\\n\\nFor the example in the QA thread, please share the question and incorrect fact, as requested there, so we can assess whether the fact drives the final answer.\", \"scope_note\": \"Restate the current criterion only; leave the incomplete examples ungraded and keep the request for supporting details scoped to the QA thread.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c1\", \"c2\", \"c3\", \"c4\", \"c6\", \"c7\", \"c8\"], \"targets\": [], \"context_claim_ids\": [\"c5\", \"c9\", \"c10\"]}, \"severity\": {\"level\": \"MEDIUM\", \"rationale\": \"Repeated uncertainty about the factual-error threshold, alongside a QA tutor's reported mismatch between an example's grade and its effect on the recommendation, could lead to inconsistent scoring. The messages do not establish broader disruption.\", \"signals\": [{\"level\": \"MEDIUM\", \"signal_index\": 0, \"signal_text\": \"Recurring confusion about the same rule, tool behavior, or scoring criterion that suggests meaningful workflow or labeling impact\", \"support\": \"Two tutors separately ask what makes a factual error significant, and a QA tutor reports that an example labeled minor changes the final recommendation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\"]}], \"affected_reporters\": [{\"author_id\": \"U007\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\"}], \"recurrence\": \"NONE_FOUND\", \"recurrence_evidence_ids\": [], \"reported_recurrence_evidence_ids\": []}, \"confidence\": 0.88, \"open_confirmation\": \"NONE\", \"open_question\": null, \"open_question_evidence_ids\": [], \"source_conflicts\": [{\"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\"], \"description\": \"A QA tutor reports that an example labeled minor changes the final recommendation, whereas the current FAQ defines that effect as significant. This remains a reported discrepancy, not a verified contradiction in the rubric, because the example and original question have not been provided.\"}], \"announcement_assessments\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790936513.000019:8237860f\", \"relevant\": false, \"directive\": true, \"directive_quote\": \"Please keep examples in this thread while we check the scope.\", \"rationale\": \"The announcement concerns the same project and batch but a different problem: factuality versus instruction adherence. Its direction collects examples for that discussion; it does not govern the significance threshold or establish a route for assessing these reports.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\", \"relevant\": false, \"directive\": true, \"directive_quote\": \"Bring both rationales for disputed pairs to the eight-pair calibration review.\", \"rationale\": \"The announcement directs a tie-calibration exercise in batch 14, not handling of factual-error significance questions in batch 15.\"}], \"resolution\": [{\"member_id\": \"member_953da9c9fb3c542a10ba503d\", \"state\": \"UNRESOLVED\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\"], \"basis\": \"The tutor asks for the significance threshold; a tutor discusses event order and the need for the original question, but the thread does not settle the threshold or the example.\"}, {\"member_id\": \"member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"state\": \"PARTIALLY_RESOLVED\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\"], \"basis\": \"The team lead establishes what information is needed next, but the retrieved thread contains neither those inputs nor a final assessment of the QA tutor's example.\"}, {\"member_id\": \"member_c6c1dd006877c443863522d1\", \"state\": \"UNRESOLVED\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\"], \"basis\": \"The tutor's significance question receives a tutor's example and a QA tutor's diagnostic question, but no final answer or confirmed grade.\"}], \"coverage\": [{\"need\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"status\": \"COVERED\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\"], \"note\": \"Current project-wide instructions and FAQ agree on the factual-error criterion.\", \"gap_id\": null}, {\"need\": \"ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"status\": \"COVERED\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790936513.000019:8237860f\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-post@1.0:4a3c786f\"], \"note\": \"Both retrieved announcements were assessed; neither governs this batch's factual-error significance question.\", \"gap_id\": null}, {\"need\": \"PRIOR_DECISIONS\", \"status\": \"MISSING\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:053fe48a\"], \"note\": \"The follow-up retrieved approval and outcome records for batch-14 tie calibration, not earlier handling of significant factual errors or the reported minor example. That history remains a gap but is not needed to restate current guidance.\", \"gap_id\": \"g1\"}, {\"need\": \"MEMBER_QUESTIONS\", \"status\": \"COVERED\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914946.000024\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790914994.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790915039.000226\"], \"note\": \"The threads show repeated threshold questions, contrasting date examples, diagnostic questions, and the team lead's thread-scoped request.\", \"gap_id\": null}], \"review_note\": null, \"action_choice\": null}, \"evidence\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866580.000020\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_953da9c9fb3c542a10ba503d\", \"thread_id\": \"1790866580.000020\", \"author_id\": \"U017\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T14:56:20.000020Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Anyone else seeing this? Rubric says significant factual error; how big is significant?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790866638.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_953da9c9fb3c542a10ba503d\", \"thread_id\": \"1790866580.000020\", \"author_id\": \"U020\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T14:57:18.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The wrong date changes which event happened first; that seems central. The evaluator needs the original question before deciding whether this fact is central.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870514.000021\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"thread_id\": \"1790870514.000021\", \"author_id\": \"U007\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T16:01:54.000021Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Rubric example calls this minor, but it changes the final recommendation.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870569.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"thread_id\": \"1790870514.000021\", \"author_id\": \"U013\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T16:02:49.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"thumbsup\", \"users\": [\"U020\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"If that incorrect date changes the recommendation, the impact is substantive rather than just background detail.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870609.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_b1d306767d2a8f697f21699c\", \"thread_id\": \"1790870514.000021\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T16:03:29.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Is the date essential to the requested result or only background context?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790870662.000339\", \"orig